  "music": "w2-sizzle-street",
  "authorNotes": "Two players, three checkpoints, four segments — every mechanic Sizzle Street has, back to back. relic-tuna is picked up at spawn (330,935) and carried the whole run. Seg 1: a plain swing (swing-gauntlet-1, 270px), gets both players moving. Seg 2 combines the belt and the pan again (06's escalation, reused at full length): belt-gauntlet-2 (1600,960 to 2050,960, 450px, no plank) carries you through pan-gauntlet's grace window (1780,960, 1.2s) automatically, or rope-gauntlet-2 (anchor 1900,600) lets a cautious pair grab clear of it. Seg 3 is the hardest: pier B (2050-2750) to pier C (3160-3760) is 410px, the world's team-gate gap again, solved the same way as 07 — swing-anchor-gauntlet (pivot 2955,700) anchors one player while the other is thrown across, and pier C's near edge is a grease landing strip, so the throw alone is not enough; someone needs to already be planted to catch the landing. relic-rice waits just past the grease (3450,850). Seg 4 is two short belt hops with a grease patch on the pier D landing (4150-4350) and relic-nori (4300,820) sitting past it, then swing-final-gauntlet (300px) onto the goal pier, where plate-sashimi (4950,790) takes all three ingredients for the Sashimi Three Ways recipe objective. All four true gaps carry an assist beam (the seg-3 one drawn thicker, same convention as the team gate) for a party trading the Clock objective for a guaranteed finish this deep into the level."
